sequenceDiagram
  %% ADR 0266 slice 4; docs/reference/executor.md#rust-sleep-and-discard. Proof-only durable power orders, never production instance.sleep.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · started by proof support on a nested Gateway
  %% kind: executor.power_proof
  autonumber
  %% lane RN icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane OB icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane EX icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant RN as Proof runner
  participant GW as Nested Gateway
  participant OB as Observer<br/>orbit-agent
  participant EX as Executor<br/>app-dev Node
  RN->>GW: Sleep or discard INSTANCE
  %%> Caller:
  %%> - only tools/swamp-proof-guest/executor-order.php, as the Gateway's managed user
  Note over GW: Record running Operation<br/>Instance target, node_id
  GW->>OB: Signed executor-order
  OB->>EX: Order bytes, unread
  %%> Admission:
  %%> - caller, signature, enabled family, Node and target checks precede work
  alt sleep
    Note over EX: Limits, Incus freeze<br/>scan whole subtree, publish plan
    %%> Durable state:
    %%> - atomically fsync non-max swap limits before opening them, and the plan before reclaim
    %%> - parallel maps/pagemap capture includes bits 63 and 62; recovery preserves a valid published plan
    Note over EX: Reclaim, residual policy<br/>write asleep marker last
    %%> Outcome:
    %%> - memory.current settles or 2 s pass; at most 32 MiB anonymous RAM may remain
    %%> - otherwise unfreeze and stop; a nested fleet resumes and fails instead
    %%> Failure:
    %%> - retain frozen recovery state; a refused freeze restores the original swap limits
  else discard
    Note over EX: Drop plan and limits
    %%> Scope:
    %%> - after stop, destroy or fresh boot; repeating removal is safe
  end
  EX-->>OB: Journaled result
  %%> Execution:
  %%> - per-target lock; a repeated Operation returns its first result without running again
  OB->>GW: Result bytes, unread
  GW->>GW: Record and hand off result<br/>close Operation
  %%> Outcome:
  %%> - succeeded on done, failed otherwise; a throw closes all open proof Operations
  GW-->>RN: Durable result and timings
